# UST.G3BN H11 Alternate Split-Prime Initializer Theorem

## Result

The selected H11 chart at the G3BI root-containing endpoint is invertible over
`Q(gamma)`. G3BN proves this by exact reduction at the completely split place

```text
(21817, gamma-5).
```

The resulting `5439 x 5439` endpoint chart has

```text
determinant = 276 mod 21817,
```

which is nonzero. This closes the characteristic-zero H11 endpoint chart-
existence question left by G3BK and resolves the G3BL proof-prime obstruction.

## Construction

Start from the hash-certified selected B89 H11 chart evaluated at
`(21817,gamma-5)`. Its 5,439 columns consist of

```text
1013 quotient units + 4426 selected original-Jacobian columns.
```

G3BN reconstructs the G3BI correction `C` from all 19 exact `Q(gamma)` terms,
differentiates `sC` in all ten Cayley variables, evaluates at the split place,
and compiles the result in the same 4,426 selected-column order. The finite
endpoint chart is therefore exactly

```text
A_G3BI = A_B89 + Delta_C.
```

The correction update has 18,748 nonzero entries at this place. An independent
verifier rebuilds this update from the number-field coefficients, reconstructs
the endpoint chart byte for byte, and reruns the sparse modular factorization.

## Why One Split Root Suffices

Every selected-chart entry belongs to `Z[gamma]`, so its determinant is an
element of `Z[gamma]`. If that determinant were zero in `Q(gamma)`, every good
reduction at every root of the minimal polynomial would be zero. The displayed
nonzero reduction therefore proves

```text
det(A_G3BI) != 0 in Q(gamma).
```

No CRT reconstruction of the determinant is needed for this existence claim.
CRT is still required to recover a large inverse action over `Q(gamma)` from
modular solutions.

## Relation To G3BL

G3BL proved that the same endpoint presentation has corank one at
`(11,gamma-3)`, even after every unused original-Jacobian column is restored.
G3BN shows that this is bad reduction of the finite presentation:

```text
GF(11), gamma=3:      rank 5438/5439,
GF(21817), gamma=5:   rank 5439/5439.
```

Thus the G3BI endpoint and its H11 characteristic-zero chart survive. The
correct transport implementation initializes H11 through an admissible split
place such as G3BN, while retaining G3BK's algebraic-pole avoidance on the
transcendental interior.

